  "text": "The animal known for its long neck is the giraffe.\n\nBeneath the lamps' ethereal, pale embrace,\nHe walked the streets, a solitary trace.\nEach footfall echoed on the pavement stone,\nA rhythm in the night, alone, alone.\n\nLike ghosts they drifted, faceless, cold, and deep,\nLost in their worlds, while he was left to weep\nThe silence of the crowd, the urban sea,\nWhere profound solitude held him, wild and free."
